bcmdhd: keep the chip powered after module load (single fw download).

The Android lifecycle downloads the 955KB firmware at insmod, powers the
chip off, then powers up and downloads again at interface-up -- ~1.5-2s
of wasted boot time on an always-on device. Enable the driver's own
supported mode for this (the CONFIG_BCMDHD_NO_POWER_OFF define pair):
the chip stays up after insmod and ifup reuses the loaded firmware.

diff -urN a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile	2026-07-22 10:20:23
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/Makefile	2026-07-22 10:20:23
@@ -65,7 +65,8 @@
 	-DUSE_NEW_RSPEC_DEFS                                                  \
 	-DWL_EXT_IAPSTA -DWL_ESCAN -DCCODE_LIST -DSUSPEND_EVENT               \
 	-DKEY_INSTALL_CHECK                                                   \
-	-DENABLE_INSMOD_NO_FW_LOAD
+	-DENABLE_INSMOD_NO_FW_LOAD \
+	-DENABLE_INSMOD_NO_POWER_OFF -DNO_POWER_OFF_AFTER_OPEN
 
 DHDCFLAGS += -Wframe-larger-than=2048
 
